Article 28
(1) The Regent implements policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of Violence Against Women.
(2) Regional Apparatus with responsibility for Women implements policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women that have been established and their implementation is carried out in cooperation and coordination with related Regional Apparatus, law enforcement, community institutions, universities, and the community.
(3) The implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be in the form of:
a. policy analysis;
b. advocacy;
c. coordination and communication;
d. socialization;
e. education;
f. training;
g. facilitation;
h. provision of services; and
i. other forms.
